      "description": "Tianhao Luo is a PhD student in Biomedical Informatics at Harvard Medical School and an NSF Graduate Research Fellow in AI for Life Sciences. He builds multi-modal foundation models and generative models for biology and medicine — AI virtual cells and AI virtual patients, spatial and single-cell genomics — to understand disease mechanisms and translate them into clinically actionable insights. He is also the founder of MedJourney, an AI-powered voice-first companion for Alzheimer's patients, and of a stealth AI startup in healthcare and precision medicine. He graduated summa cum laude from the University of Pennsylvania with a B.S. in Statistics from The Wharton School and a B.A. in Mathematics and Computational Biology.",
